{
  "run_id": "PMC11077685__scimon__niche_ground_b_o3mini__s2",
  "auditor": "trapi:gpt-5.6-sol_2026-07-09",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Poor oxidation resistance is a major obstacle to using refractory high-entropy alloys in high-temperature applications.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6513993::chunk::001::introduction::4b945ce700",
        "PMC7475834::chunk::001::introduction::97cd4ea6cb"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Atomic layer deposition can produce a precisely controlled surface coating.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "An ALD coating will form a continuous and dense protective oxide during high-temperature oxidation.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Formation of a stable protective oxide layer can improve the high-temperature oxidation resistance of an RHEA.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6513993::chunk::001::introduction::4b945ce700"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The coating composition and thickness can be optimized for high-temperature oxidation conditions.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed treatment is intended for oxidative exposure around 1000–1100 °C for long durations.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The ALD coating may form a dense CrTaO4-based or similarly stable oxide.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The coating-derived oxide acts as a diffusion barrier against oxygen ingress.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "ALD provides nanometer-scale control over coating parameters.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A stable and continuous coating-derived oxide restricts oxygen diffusion into the bulk alloy.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Restricting oxygen diffusion into the alloy mitigates further substrate oxidation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "ALD-coated RHEA samples will have a lower oxidation rate than uncoated samples under identical conditions.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reduced weight gain will indicate reduced oxidation.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "ALD-coated RHEAs will exhibit better oxide-scale integrity than uncoated RHEAs.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxidation-resistance benefit requires the coating to remain dense, continuous, and adherent at high temperature.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Loss of coating integrity can diminish the protective effect.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The magnitude of improvement depends on coating composition, thickness, and long-term stability.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Optimal coating parameters may differ among RHEA compositions.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The hypothesis can be tested by comparing coated and uncoated RHEAs after isothermal oxidation at 1100 °C for 200 hours.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.design",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Failure to obtain a statistically significant oxidation reduction or a continuous protective oxide would falsify the hypothesis.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.falsification_rule",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    }
